    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30fa1817_aed75eb8",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 758,
      "author": {
        "id": 1374565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-15T06:13:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When refreshZramSettings() enables ZRAM, we might run into a timing issue. ZramWriteback checks the backingdev node to figure out if writeback is enabled. However backingdev is not written until fs_mgr parses fstab and sets up the zram device.\nOne possible way is that I could make the assumption that writeback is enabled if config_zramWriteback is true. backingdev need not be read and since the job scheduled into the future, zram device would be ready. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "681b96ab_6fbb85fb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 756,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 758,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "2ab70e335efd8294a706ec2f0a5d7ca601306276",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "506e3d00_ab852053",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 758,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275554
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-15T07:31:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the call order between setup zram swap setup by fs_mgr and this handleSystemReady?\nCan we make sure initial triggering of zram writeback in vendor?\nWhat I meant is once vendor set up zram swap, they could trigger this working logic for initial idle page marking and schedule next writeback.",
      "parentUuid": "30fa1817_aed75eb8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 756,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 758,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "2ab70e335efd8294a706ec2f0a5d7ca601306276",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "766f2a33_f83d7a11",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/StorageManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 758,
      "author": {
        "id": 1374565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-15T17:23:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In regular boot cases, handleSystemReady is called after zram swap is setup. In cases where persist.sys.zram_enabled is disabled at boot, swapon_all is not triggered until persist.sys.zram_enabled is set to 1 by refreshZramSettings(). Once the property is set, init code calls swapon_all which sets up the zram swap.\nRegarding moving the initial trigger to vendor code, I prefer all writeback logic to be in one place so that it does not depend on vendor implementation details.",
      "parentUuid": "506e3d00_ab852053",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 756,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 758,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "2ab70e335efd8294a706ec2f0a5d7ca601306276",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
